    ("gov_m6_49", "International Relations: High Commissioner", "1999", "Why are diplomatic representatives between Commonwealth member states called High Commissioners rather than Ambassadors?", ["Because Commonwealth members share historical ties and do not treat each other as complete foreign foreign entities", "Because High Commissioners have higher diplomatic rank than Ambassadors", "Because they are directly elected by the public", "Because they can vote in the host country's parliament"], 0, "Historically, Commonwealth nations owed allegiance to a common British Crown, making their representatives special Commissioners between governments.", "Medium"),
